.TH PIC 1
.SH NAME
pic \- draw pictures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pic
[
.B -V
] [
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pic
is a preprocessor for
.IR troff (1):
each picture in its
.I files
(or its standard input), between
.B .PS
and
.BR .PE ,
is turned into troff's drawing commands; the rest is passed on.
A picture is described in Kernighan's language of boxes, circles,
ellipses, arcs, lines, arrows and splines, placed by one another and
labelled, with variables,
.BR for ,
.BR if ,
.BR define
and blocks:
.IP
.EX
\&.PS
box "input"; arrow; ellipse "pic"; arrow; box "troff"
\&.PE
.EE
.PP
It is a translation of Plan 9's
.IR pic ;
for the same input its output is, byte for byte, Plan 9's.
.TP
.B -V
Print the version.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/pic
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR troff (1)
.br
B. W. Kernighan, \(lqPIC \(em A Graphics Language for Typesetting\(rq.
